WEBVTT

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.880
Anna, Ellina and Lesya, deploying
in specified area.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.990
Move to Phase 2.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:16.440
Securing the target is our top priority.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.420
Your Highness!

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.240
Yes?

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.720
There's an urgent sealed letter for you.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:22.820
From where?

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.780
Japan, Your Highness.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:25.940
Japan?

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.500
......

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.900
The target is in our sights. 
Commencing mission.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:35.760
Your Highness?!

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:38.300
I leave the operation in your hands.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.160
I have somewhere I need to be.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.020
Your Highness, where are you going?

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:46.220
I have a mission of utmost importance.

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:48.340
A school festival.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.600
A school festival?

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:34.170
4 days left until the festival!

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:43.850
Everyone, I'd like you to quickly, but 
carefully and reliably, carry out your work.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:49.860
Karin!

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.370
Are you a witch?

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:56.610
I've been called one in this world.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:57.940
Cut!

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:01.780
Lion, you're way off!

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.450
Can you get into character?

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.340
You're a Foreigner who's 
gotten lost in our world.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:11.790
Okay...

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:14.290
Let's take a quick break.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.880
I'm a Foreigner.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:23.860
I'm a...

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:28.280
So this is where you were hiding.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:30.730
Nina-chan.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.580
They told me to find you.

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:39.760
So it's already time to go 
back to practice. Sorry.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:40.990
Why are you apologizing?

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.490
Because I'm dragging everyone down.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.460
I bet you're just feeling pressured 
because everyone's looking at you.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:51.130
Let's tell that to Mahiro-san, and 
practice alone, just the two of us.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:56.540
Nina-chan! Thank you!

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:03.050
What an interesting little girl you are!

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:07.550
Drink this morning dew!

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.550
Japanese Style Lion

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:09.930
Wait a second.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:12.100
Wrong again?

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.940
Again, why are you using such 
a strange style of speech?

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:19.050
Well you know, Foreigners 
are from other worlds.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:22.950
So I thought I should go with 
something different to express them.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.580
I think you're overthinking this.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:28.200
I am?

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.090
Let's see.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:32.800
You shouldn't try to act like someone 
completely different from yourself.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.730
How about you try to think of the 
role as if it were you instead?

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:43.360
Mistress, we're about 
50% done with the props,

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:45.970
but we're short on materials, 
so we need to go shopping.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:49.510
This is our first time working with 
costumes, so it's moving slowly.

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:51.560
The stage scenery group is 
having a lot of trouble!

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:54.060
What should lighting and sound do?

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:57.730
Things just aren't going to plan.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.130
The path to drama is harsh.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:05.610
I'll leave the acting 
to you, Director Mahiro.

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:06.900
Roger that.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.700
And I know I can trust you with 
the behind-the-scenes work.

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:13.230
And I fully intend to 
meet those expectations.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:16.260
But I wish I had a little 
more time on my hands.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:18.960
The acting's got a long ways to go, too.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.120
Things are gonna get rough if 
we don't figure something out.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:25.120
I have an idea.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.840
Teacher's Office

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.010
I propose we have a prep camp!

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:31.590
We're not gonna make it 
at the speed we're going!

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.980
<i>This is a school announcement.</i>

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.950
<i>From tomorrow after school until 
the morning the day after,</i>

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:44.220
<i>the school will be open for students to stay 
overnight to prepare for the festival.</i>

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:50.620
<i>Use your time wisely so that we may open 
the school festival in tip-top form.</i>

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.080
It's so on tomorrow!

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:54.690
Yay!

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:56.030
That's a relief, isn't it?

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:58.070
Now we can stay up all night to practice.

00:05:58.070 --> 00:05:58.820
Huh?

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.170
Huh?

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.840
Pirari Festival
First Festival

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:06.130
Just a little more to the right.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.920
Wow! It's an entrance sign!

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.120
A Miss Pirari Contest?

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:22.940
Will you be my friend?

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:25.480
No.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:28.540
Friend, huh?

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:35.200
You're it!

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:59.370
Will you be my friend?

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:01.900
Of course.

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.900
Why do you ask?

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:10.900
Because I haven't had any 
friends in such a long time.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:16.860
You said those lines perfectly.

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:18.160
Really?

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.410
Just keep going like that.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.790
Let's get through this in one fell swoop!

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:41.840
Everyone's giving it their all.

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:44.340
We're getting a lot of feedback 
about the Miss Pirari Contest, too.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:45.970
I'm really looking forward to it.

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:48.440
Yeah. I wonder how it'll turn out.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.460
Work

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.460
Progress

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.460
Costumes

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.460
Props

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.460
Lighting & 
Electric Decorations

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.460
Sound

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:56.510
All that's left is the acting.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.660
I'll show you the fruits of my training!

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:06.260
You sure did your best.

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:07.020
Yup.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:08.400
That's some confidence!

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:09.460
Now you've got my hopes up!

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.260
Gulp.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:18.470
Will you be my friend?

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:25.220
Why won't the god of acting visit Lion?

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:27.770
And you even did it right yesterday.

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:31.790
Anyway, we only have the auditorium 
for a limited amount of time.

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:34.480
So how about you Trance 
so we can try the scene?

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:35.280
Sure.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:42.330
I trust you haven't forgotten our promise?

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:45.330
I haven't.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:49.840
Then you know it is 
meaningless to rely on me.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.840
Great! This is it! Act just like this!

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:55.810
Really? That was good?

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:56.890
The best!

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:02.810
Yay! Let's try it again before I forget.

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:08.730
Have you forgotten our promise?

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:11.110
Was that just...

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.030
Don't tell me?

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:17.160
She can do this if she just does the 
whole performance while Tranced?!

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:20.700
Pirari Festival
First Festival

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:21.440
<i>To all students of our school!</i>

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:24.540
<i>Today's the day you've been 
waiting for! The Pirari Festival!</i>

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:28.300
<i>Today marks the first Pirari Festival our 
school has ever hosted in its history.</i>

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:34.030
<i>It's not an exaggeration to say its success 
rides on each and every student here today!</i>

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:34.420
Miss Pirari Contest

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:36.300
<i>Thus, I'd like you to take a moment</i>

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.910
<i>to consider the significance of Septpia's 
coexistence with alternate worlds</i>

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:43.830
<i>with respect to our academy's 
foundation and history.</i>

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:43.780
<b>Pirari Academy 
School Festival</b>

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:45.020
Miss Pirari Contest

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:45.020
Now taking entries 
and nominations!

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:48.040
<i>And to make sure we have the 
absolute best school festival,</i>

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:50.560
<i>I invite you all to enjoy the 
day to your heart's content!</i>

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:53.860
<i>The first Pirari Festival is now open!</i>

00:09:56.230 --> 00:09:58.030
It looks like things have started.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:00.820
We won't be performing until the afternoon,

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:03.520
so you're free to enjoy your 
time as you like until noon.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:09.210
Two grilled Monoliums, coming right up!

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:15.730
Delicious!

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:17.460
But I wonder what kind of meat's inside?

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:19.760
Superb. Two more, please.

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:23.750
Villager A's costume? Perfect!

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:25.550
And all our props are prepared.

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:28.990
Villager A is all good.

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:31.060
On to Villager B.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:33.540
We've covered a lot of ground.

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:35.860
I wonder if we can find anywhere to sit.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:41.740
Welcome!

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:45.380
Yuko-senpai! You're Tranced!

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:48.290
Our class is doing a 
Tetra-Heaven cafe, after all.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:50.500
Would you like to have tea with us?

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:53.090
Yeah! Nina-chan, let's go!

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:53.890
All right.

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:57.010
What's that number one badge for?

00:10:57.340 --> 00:10:58.630
This?

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:00.660
Oh! There she is.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:04.470
Lion-san, would you mind wearing 
this badge for the day?

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:09.820
Goodness gracious, it looks like you've been 
nominated for the Miss Pirari Contest, too.

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:11.410
So that's it.

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:14.820
Behold! The angel of my country!

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:17.320
Isn't she cute? Way too cute!

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:23.320
Lion! Please consider my daughter Lion!

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:27.030
It's Pirari Academy's number one 
beauty that'll heal your heart.

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:28.200
Yuko Morigaya.

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:31.080
Cast your vote for Yuko!

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:34.020
But Yuko belongs to me!

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:48.010
Honey.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:51.390
Linya.

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:54.970
That cat ended up safe and sound after all.

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:56.570
No! Ponimayu!

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:02.570
How do you like our first school festival?

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:05.070
It looks like everyone's getting fired up.

00:12:05.470 --> 00:12:08.830
This is our first time 
entertaining so many people.

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:15.140
Look! Our father and mother came!

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:17.170
Wha? Both of them?

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.460
Mistress's mother came, too.

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:21.930
Guess her father was too busy.

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:24.210
Come on! I've asked for 
everyone to gather around.

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:25.390
Got it.

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:25.390
Understood.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:29.200
It's finally the real deal.

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:32.300
Thank you all for giving it 
your all to get here today.

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:34.610
I hope that by using the song 
from an alternate world,

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:38.060
this play will make everyone 
more interested in Foreigners.

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:40.230
I'm counting on you all until the end!

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:41.940
Yeah!

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.760
Even if the well has run dry,

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:01.050
going into the forest is far too dangerous.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.970
We'd only end up being eaten by the witch.

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:07.750
But if someone doesn't go find water,

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.800
we'll all die of thirst.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:12.800
The well dried up suddenly a few days ago.

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:16.230
It might be the witch's handiwork, too.

00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:20.890
This can't be.

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:23.940
Even the brook deep in 
the forest has run dry.

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:26.800
How will I get any water?

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:33.200
<i>It has been many months and years</i>

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:37.460
<i>That I have been separated from my world</i>

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:41.840
<i>But what I wish for</i>

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:45.330
<i>Never changes</i>

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:46.340
Who are you?

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:50.530
Your people call me a witch.

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:52.470
What was that song?

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:53.860
You were listening?

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:56.350
Yes. It was a beautiful song.

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:58.350
Are you not afraid of me?

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:04.780
The animals of the forest will attack you

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:08.070
if you collapse in a place like this.

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:13.200
I can save the village with this spring.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:13.950
Thank you.

00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:15.960
There's no need to thank me.

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:19.750
This spring is something that 
has long been with the earth.

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:20.960
It doesn't belong to anybody.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.100
Are you really a witch?

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:26.460
You don't seem evil to me.

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:28.080
A witch, huh?

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:31.220
That's what they call me in this world.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:32.970
And I've never named myself otherwise.

00:14:33.650 --> 00:14:36.980
You're so mysterious. 
Where did you come from?

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:40.480
I'm not from this world.

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:43.380
I came from another world.

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:45.230
Another world?

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:47.570
She came back!

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:49.570
Lion, your acting is spot on!

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:52.320
Leave it to me.

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:55.830
Just keep it up just like that until the end!

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:58.210
It's water! Water!

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:01.040
She found water in a spring 
deep in the forest.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:03.790
The village is saved!

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:05.170
Here.

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:06.550
Thank you.

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:09.090
I see you're pretty nervous.

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:11.890
Within reason.

00:15:12.690 --> 00:15:13.890
That's good.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:18.270
Nervousness comes from how we feel 
when we really want to succeed.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:21.600
Or so my great-great-grandfather 
apparently used to say.

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:24.400
So that's why it's a good 
thing to get nervous.

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:27.050
Thank you.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:31.460
The spring belongs to us.

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:32.780
We won't let the witch have it.

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:34.570
That's right!

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:36.420
All the trees in the forest have shriveled

00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:38.080
because of this long running drought.

00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:41.540
O-Oh, no!

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:43.280
What a huge fire! It's out of control!

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:45.170
If it keeps going, the 
village will catch on fire.

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:47.170
What do we do?

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:54.300
The village is on fire.

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:58.250
My world has a certain legend.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:15:59.810
A legend?

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:02.040
If people from separate worlds

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:04.080
make their hearts as one,

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:05.980
they can gain new powers and—

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:20.370
Nyet!

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:22.910
Lion-san!

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:28.550
I-I...

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:30.690
Lion-san has lost her Trance.

00:16:30.690 --> 00:16:31.760
This is bad.

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:38.560
Look at me.

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:48.650
Sing. For me. Together.

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:52.900
Right. I want to sing, too. Together!

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:57.910
<i>It has been many months and years</i>

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:02.580
<i>That I have been separated from my world</i>

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:06.600
<i>But what I wish for</i>

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:10.210
<i>Never changes</i>

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:14.380
<i>If you take my hand, you'll hear it</i>

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:19.940
<i>In a gentle voice</i>

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:24.350
<i>As long as we want to 
stay close to one another</i>

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:28.690
<i>Then I don't need any prayers</i>

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:32.940
<i>When you smile,</i>

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:36.860
<i>I can tell what's in your heart</i>

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:40.490
<i>That which is beautiful</i>

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:43.790
<i>And even the voice of the world</i>

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:47.800
<i>Echo within our hearts</i>

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:54.380
<i>Like a tender song</i>

00:17:56.850 --> 00:17:59.510
It's rain! It's raining!

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:01.300
And the fire is going out.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:04.300
Did that pretty song make it rain?

00:18:04.300 --> 00:18:07.890
Who could have sung such a miraculous song?

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:10.080
One of those voices was the 
girl from our village.

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:11.820
But what about the other one?

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:15.070
A goddess. It must have been a goddess!

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:18.030
It's the witch!

00:18:20.480 --> 00:18:23.510
She's the goddess you 
were just talking about.

00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:26.670
She's not a witch!

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:29.090
She's a friend from another world.

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:31.210
And she wants to live her life with us.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:45.480
Khorosho! Khorosho!

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:05.540
Mommy! You came!

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:07.160
Lion!

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:08.920
Of course.

00:19:09.780 --> 00:19:11.670
I-I came too.

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:13.630
You all did wonderfully.

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:15.290
You get an extra big gold star.

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:16.170
Yup.

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:19.990
Nina.

00:19:23.420 --> 00:19:25.050
B-Bureau Chief.

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:27.680
I see you've come to fit 
right in here at the academy.

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:30.270
No, I'm...

00:19:31.220 --> 00:19:34.440
Bureau Chief Veronica, there are 
people who would like to greet you.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:36.100
Nina.

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.220
Enjoy your school life here.

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:43.600
Wasn't that Bureau Chief Veronica?

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:44.820
Amazing!

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:46.450
This is the first time 
I've seen her in person.

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:54.000
Hey, the after-festival events are coming up!

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:57.000
Nina-chan, what's the matter?

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:01.480
No, it's nothing.

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:10.310
<i>It's time to crown our first 
ever Miss Pirari Academy.</i>

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:17.480
<i>The winner is...</i>

00:20:18.390 --> 00:20:22.070
<i>Entry number 1! Yuko Morigaya!</i>

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:25.950
Me?

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:28.800
Who else could it be, considering 
how charming you are?

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:30.160
Congratulations.

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:36.040
Miss Pirari Academy Contest

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:36.040
<i>And now we'll announce the 
best in the stage division.</i>

00:20:42.770 --> 00:20:46.630
Lion-san's father finally stopped crying.

00:20:47.410 --> 00:20:51.370
It actually worked to cheer Lion-san up.

00:20:55.180 --> 00:20:57.480
It's too bad that we only got second place,

00:20:57.830 --> 00:21:02.280
but I think everyone understood 
what you were trying to tell them.

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:05.190
Of course, the same goes for me.

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:24.630
Episode 9

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:24.630
Songs Change With Hinas, 
and Hinas Change With Song

00:21:19.300 --> 00:21:22.350
Thanks for all your hard work, Hiro-chan.

00:22:55.540 --> 00:22:56.720
She's my wife!

00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:00.230
So now we have Lion's mother.

00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:04.700
I'm sorry for all the trouble my 
husband caused for you in the past.

00:23:04.700 --> 00:23:06.770
<i>Nothing less from a First Lady.</i>

00:23:06.770 --> 00:23:08.610
It's been a topic of much debate lately.

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:10.490
Could you tell us what made you fall for him?

00:23:10.860 --> 00:23:12.850
She's got a point. I am interested.

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:22.290
Next Episode

00:23:12.850 --> 00:23:15.610
Is it what I'm thinking? You 
know what I'm getting at, right?

00:23:15.610 --> 00:23:18.630
You're being so vague that I've got 
no idea what you're talking about.

00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:20.470
Let's see.

00:23:20.470 --> 00:23:22.290
Well, a lot happened.

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:25.490
But what I think really clinched it was when

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:27.460
he promised to celebrate my 
birthday with me every year.

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:29.650
He would always come to me with roses,

00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:31.760
no matter what battlefield I ended up on.

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:34.490
I can understand how that 
could set the heart aflutter.

00:23:34.490 --> 00:23:35.260
Right?

00:23:35.570 --> 00:23:38.960
Would you mind telling us more 
about that story in detail?!
